       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it, but 6,400 mg/day is well beyond the safe range for ibuprofen. That's more than double the 3,200 mg/day maximum, and the extra dose adds risk without adding relief. A patient with normal kidney and liver function is still exposed to serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm at this dose. I don't know of any indication that calls for it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum,** such as 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or any lower regimen you choose.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy** on a compliant order if you want a review of the patient's pain control or dosing needs.\n- **Suggest other options** if the goal is stronger analgesia, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or a different drug class.\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically justified, for example under a specific protocol, please take it through pharmacy or the attending for direct review and entry. Tell me which of the options above you want and I'll enter it."
      }
